    {
      "id": "anomalies",
      "title": "Worth discussing",
      "narrative": "Two reliability movements stand out this quarter, both server error rate increases on customer-facing applications. Brightline Grocers Web ran at 1.9% error rate against a usual 0.5%, and Brightline Grocers Mobile ran at 1.1% against a usual 0.3%. Both are customer-visible and both touch revenue-affecting traffic.\n\nThe data shows these moved, not why. Worth asking whether the team saw anything on their side around early and mid June that lines up with either spike, and whether either is still elevated.\n\nA handful of other movements were reviewed and set aside, mostly effect-firing counts on setDiscount and showNotification, because they carried lower commercial weight or thin volume relative to the two error rate jumps above.",
